A. Commit message:
platform/x86: asus-nb-wmi: Ignore unknown event 0xCF

B. Change summary:
Added an entry to ignore the unknown event 0xCF in the keymap for Asus notebooks. This event is emitted when the charger is plugged in on certain models, such as the Asus X541UAK. Ignoring this event silences unnecessary warnings.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/asus-nb-wmi.c b/drivers/platform/x86/asus-nb-wmi.c
index ef04d396f61c7..a5933980ade3d 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/asus-nb-wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/asus-nb-wmi.c
@@ -623,6 +623,7 @@ static const struct key_entry asus_nb_wmi_keymap[] = {
 	{ KE_KEY, 0xC4, { KEY_KBDILLUMUP } },
 	{ KE_KEY, 0xC5, { KEY_KBDILLUMDOWN } },
 	{ KE_IGNORE, 0xC6, },  /* Ambient Light Sensor notification */
+	{ KE_IGNORE, 0xCF, },	/* AC mode */
 	{ KE_KEY, 0xFA, { KEY_PROG2 } },           /* Lid flip action */
 	{ KE_KEY, 0xBD, { KEY_PROG2 } },           /* Lid flip action on ROG xflow laptops */
 	{ KE_END, 0},
```